## Read-only overlap rescout (2026-08-25)

The changed-equipment screen is complete against the last checked-in candidate basis. It found no installed six-plugin projections in the current global route, so no equipment was silently migrated or dropped. The scan produced candidate evidence only; it did not change plugin content or qualification state.

Recommended dispositions for operator review are:

- carry Rolecasting dispatch/reconciliation, Tricritical projections, Mergecraft review/publication safeguards, and the common six-plugin release-boundary validators as one dependent closure;
- carry Versionkeeping publication/credential changes, Task Witness runtime/qualification changes, and the cross-family source-stage gate only through their separate Daybreak security lanes;
- hold Thermos-derived behavior until its rule-level source/destination map exists;
- retain Matt Pocock-managed skills side-by-side and compare only the explicitly maintained Versionkeeping derivative; and
- use superseded Superpowers routes for semantic-drift and absence evidence, not as new plugin equipment.

No final rescout or release-qualification claim is made until Ivan reviews these dispositions and accepted changes are reconciled with fresh locks and dependent evidence.

